  "about": [
    "Every route's ceilings, the one table (17 Oct 2026; the coordinator's rule: one source of route ceilings). A line for every page and layout under app/.",
    "source: bytes of source the file reaches by static import (a dynamic import() is a chunk of its own and isn't followed), measured by scripts/fluidity/reach.mjs and held by app/firstLoad.test.ts on every quick check, with no build. A layout's line is the layout's own reach. A page's line is its route's (since V-49, 29 Oct 2026): the page with every layout and boundary in its folder and each folder above it (reach.mjs routeReach), once each, since every visit loads them all; moving an import from a page into its layout no longer lowers it.",
    "gzipKB: a page's first-load script in a production build, gzip -9, with the runtime and every entry segment on its path (layouts, templates, not-found, global-error, error and loading boundaries, and metadata entries, whose chunk the HTML lists too), as its HTML lists them, measured and held by scripts/fluidity/routes.mjs --check after the build (the integrator's full gate).",
    "beyondHome: the doc route's source beyond Home's, as app/app/doc/docFirstLoad.test.ts has held it since 12 Oct (docs A1).",
    "The rule (main's V-49 amendment, 29 Oct 2026; scripts/fluidity/routes.mjs headroom, lineFor and lineProblem): every line, source and gzip, page and non-page, and beyondHome, is its measure plus headroom, max(2 KB, 1%) for a source line and max(1 KB, 1%) for a gzip line (KB = 1,024 B). Lines never rise: growth past the headroom needs main's yes, with a shipped-bytes reason. A line more than twice its headroom above its measure fails app/firstLoad.test.ts (source) and routes.mjs --check (gzip), saying where to ratchet it down to: the head that shrank a route lowers its own line. A new page takes its line before its first gate (routes.mjs --propose prints every line by the rule).",
    "edition: \"ai\" marks a page only the AI edition has; the edition without AI keeps the line and has no page for it.",
    "target, where a programme set one, is where the route must get to, and owner the package that gets it there.",
    "Measured on 29 Oct 2026 (V-49) on web beta b9762d229 (wE30, its landing beta), with a production build pinned to one build ID before and after, whose HTML-listed JS was byte for byte the same (159 scripts over five pages, 1,965,468 B): 108 lines (90 pages, 18 layouts and boundaries), source measures 143,478,628 B, gzip measures 44,997 KB over 92 routes, and the doc route's source beyond Home 733,108 B. Each line is its measure plus headroom; the exact lines of the first re-measure, and the 27 Oct raise before them, are gone with their slack."
